# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  📊 MONITORING STACK — Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  This file contains all the environment variables needed by the monitoring
#  stack. Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values:
#
#    cp .env.example .env
#    nano .env
#
#  ⚠️  NEVER commit your .env file to Git! It contains secrets.
#     The .env.example file is safe to commit — it only has placeholders.
#
#  ── BEFORE YOU START ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  ✅ Make sure you have a registered domain name
#  ✅ Set up Cloudflare DNS (or your DNS provider) to point your domain
#     to your server's public IP
#  ✅ Generate a strong password for Grafana (use: openssl rand -base64 32)
#  ✅ If using email alerts: create a Gmail App Password
#     (Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification → App Passwords)
#  ✅ If using Discord alerts: create a webhook in your Discord server
#     (Server Settings → Integrations → Webhooks → New Webhook)
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Domain Configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your base domain name. This is used to generate service URLs:
#   • Grafana will be at: https://monitor.example.com
#   • Uptime Kuma will be at: https://status.example.com
DOMAIN=example.com

# ── Grafana Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The admin password for Grafana's web interface.
# Generate a strong password: openssl rand -base64 32
# You'll use this to log in at https://monitor.example.com
GRAFANA_PASSWORD=change_me_strong_password

# Alertmanager does not expand Compose .env variables inside its bind-mounted
# YAML configuration. Start with the local-only receiver, then follow the
# monitoring guide to add and validate notification credentials separately.
